    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.49954642804422417,
        "y0": 0.5871808092203348,
        "x1": 0.8881040040450078,
        "y1": 0.6030243071802448
      },
      "text": "Fig. 12. ePrivacy Directive transposition into EU MSs legislation.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "list",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.498079881436376,
        "y0": 0.7078584968224098,
        "x1": 0.8979784152259147,
        "y1": 0.7739917141516879
      },
      "text": "(i) The strictest category prescribes the opt-in mechanism – i.e., the user must provide consent. The consent must be obtained before cookies are used. This interpretation is in force in 11 EU MSs.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "list",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.498079881436376,
        "y0": 0.7733743531973853,
        "x1": 0.8956635226421635,
        "y1": 0.8558865346204073
      },
      "text": "(ii) More ﬂexible interpretations allow the consent to be implied – i.e., inferred from the behavior of the user. In other words, consent can be conveyed by clicking a link or scrolling through a website. In 9 MSs, regulations allow implied consent.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.49668893001449926,
        "y0": 0.8567458002751714,
        "x1": 0.8981833621745487,
        "y1": 0.905882692556403
      },
      "text": "(iii) Tolerant interpretations of the ePrivacy Directive do not require consent. The website must show a Cookie Bar warning users about the use of cookies, that can",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    }
  ],
